Sval: open no Picture-in-Picture player for a tab an agent controls

The player window's controls play, pause, seek and mute the page's video,
and take the user's input in a window of their own, so a tab an agent
controls (the SvalAgentInControl browsing context field, which Sval's chrome
sets) gets no player. Every way to open one, the toggle, the context menu,
the shortcut, switching tabs and HTMLVideoElement.requestPictureInPicture(),
asks handlePictureInPictureRequest; the page's request rejects as when the
player does not start.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
index e1cc8e0c1d..4829e6611e 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
@@ -973,6 +973,12 @@ export var PictureInPicture = {
    *   the player component inside it has finished loading.
    */
   async handlePictureInPictureRequest(wgp, videoData) {
+    // Sval: a page in a tab an agent controls opens no player the user's
+    // input would reach.
+    if (wgp.browsingContext.top.svalAgentInControl) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     const isApiRequest = !!videoData.isPipApiRequest;
 
     if (isApiRequest) {
